# Example local.config for kali-nethunter-kernel-builder
# Copy to: $KERNEL_DIR/local.config (kernel source root, next to builder clone)
#
# Docs: docs/phases/05-build-kernel-detailed.md

# --- Target device ---
DEVICE_CODENAME=porsche
# Realme GT 2 (RMX3311 EU), SM8350, A/B slots — confirm paths in device tree

# --- Architecture ---
ARCH=arm64

# --- Defconfig (PLACEHOLDER — set after cloning kernel + matching ROM branch) ---
# Examples (verify in your tree): vendor/porsche_defconfig, lahaina_porsche_defconfig
DEFCONFIG=REPLACE_WITH_PORSCHE_DEFCONFIG

# --- Kernel image output (PLACEHOLDER — tree-dependent) ---
# Common on 5.4 GKI/vendor merges: Image, Image.gz, or Image.gz-dtb
IMAGE_NAME=Image

# DTB packaging if builder expects it (uncomment/adjust if required)
# DTBIMG=dtbo.img
# DTBOIMG=true

# --- Flash / AnyKernel (PLACEHOLDER — confirm via device tree & stock by-name) ---
# Example pattern for Realme/Oplus A/B; DO NOT flash with wrong block.
# boot_block=/dev/block/bootdevice/by-name/boot_a
# slot_device=_a
# (Menu 8 in build.sh also edits AnyKernel3 config.)

# --- Paths (optional overrides) ---
# KERNEL_DIR is usually inferred when local.config lives in kernel root.
# CLANG_PATH=...
# CROSS_COMPILE=aarch64-linux-android-

# --- Build tuning (optional) ---
# CCACHE=1
# THREADS=$(nproc)

# --- Notes ---
# 1. Run ./build.sh → S (toolchains) → 2 (build) before NetHunter patches.
# 2. Enable HID/OTG, then CONFIG_FEATURE_FRAME_INJECTION_SUPPORT, then Docker CONFIG_*.
# 3. Enable CONFIG_IKCONFIG + CONFIG_IKCONFIG_PROC for /proc/config.gz checks.
# 4. Package: build.sh → 8 (AnyKernel) → 6 (zip).
